WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
The Samsung Galaxy A56 looks almost the same as this year's more expensive models.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.240
It has excellent software and very good specifications.

3
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:13.660
Let's see whether that's enough for it to become the best buy among all Samsung models this year.

4
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:20.620
The new Galaxy A56 has landed with us, and it's clear that Samsung is sticking with a proven recipe.

5
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.940
That means the A series still looks the same as the S series.

6
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:32.340
Besides, although it doesn't seem so on paper, the real differences between the mid-range and flagships are getting smaller.

7
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.000
That is, for most users this phone is the golden mean.

8
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.180
And here's why.

9
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:45.440
The design of the A56 is almost identical to the design of the other Samsung models, from the cheapest to the most expensive,

10
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:51.060
and it's getting harder to tell apart even, say, the A36 from the S25 Ultra.

11
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.940
The moment you pick up the phone, it's clear that they didn't skimp on materials.

12
00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.460
The back panel is glass and the side frame is metal.

13
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.740
The build quality and finish are superb, and everything looks very luxurious.

14
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:10.660
The aluminum frame with two shades of matte finish stands out especially, with that ridge by the cameras, which gives away the metal even more.

15
00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:17.980
The edges are flat and, unlike the more expensive models, there is no slight curve at the edge that makes the feel in the hand more pleasant.

16
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:24.280
The A56, like its predecessor, is rather uncomfortable in the hand and seems larger than it actually is.

17
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.480
The bezel around the screen certainly contributes to this, and it could have been smaller.

18
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:37.840
In this class Samsung surely could have made a screen with a smaller bezel, which is especially noticeable at the bottom edge, so I don't know why they made such a compromise.

19
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.820
The A56 has a 6.7-inch screen, compared with 6.6 inches on the A55,

20
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.340
but the phone is also about a millimeter taller and wider.

21
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:54.260
Samsung offset the increase in size by reducing the thickness by 0.8 mm and the weight by 15 grams.

22
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.980
What you'll notice is a somewhat different camera module, whose cameras are now merged.

23
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.740
A design we haven't seen before is used here, with a cutout running under the upper ring.

24
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:14.080
It looks as if all this was stuck on top of the cameras for some reason. I think dust will accumulate there, so I'm not sure how good a solution this is.

25
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:22.460
Besides that, three camera lenses and a flash located on the side of the back panel are noticeable — another unusual design decision.

26
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:34.460
Stereo sound is supported, the upper speaker is hybrid, playback is very good, loud and clearly defined, and greatly improves the experience of multimedia content, that is, movies and series.

27
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:42.680
The fingerprint scanner is under the screen, not the fastest of those we've seen, but it works reliably, at different angles and even with wet fingers.

28
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:49.340
The phone is protected by Gorilla Glass Victus, which provides excellent scratch resistance, and even more so against drops.

29
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:56.140
Water and dust protection conforms to the IP67 standard, and everything really looks very sturdy and reliable,

30
00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.200
and the device looks very expensive when you put it down on the table like this, without a case.

31
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:10.140
The phone's screen is a flat Samsung Super AMOLED with a 6.7-inch diagonal, a 120 Hz refresh rate and a maximum brightness of 1900 nits.

32
00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:20.440
On paper that's not too much, but in practice the screen was excellent, very bright, contrasty and sharp, with a resolution of 1080×2340 pixels.

33
00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:32.200
That gives 385 pixels per inch with an 87% screen-to-body ratio, which isn't the best result because of the bezel around the screen, which, as we've already noticed, is fairly noticeable.

34
00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:41.060
The screen is impressive, and Samsung has further improved this aspect of the A series compared with last year, when they were already great in this area.

35
00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:49.380
As for the camera, the A56 continues the tradition of its predecessors: it offers basic features, but very reliable and balanced quality.

36
00:03:49.820 --> 00:04:01.000
That means it's not a camera for advanced users, but an excellent choice for all ordinary buyers who are looking for nice family shots, portraits or landscapes, pet photos — and in any conditions.

37
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.240
And they will get that.

38
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:09.040
The Samsung Galaxy A56 has a 50-megapixel main camera and a 12-megapixel ultra-wide lens,

39
00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:12.420
and also a macro lens with a 5-megapixel sensor.

40
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:20.120
The main sensor's diagonal is 1/1.56 inch, aperture f/1.8, which is more or less within the average for this segment.

41
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:26.300
The camera app is standard Samsung minimalism, without any excess in terms of filters or add-ons.

42
00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:32.500
There is, though, a fun mode, which will bring a bit of fun for young users with Snapchat filters.

43
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.400
The quality of the photos is quite correct.

44
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.900
Although Samsung used to, especially in the mid-range, process photos too heavily, making colors look oversaturated,

45
00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:48.420
now that's no longer the case, so here too, as with the more expensive models, you'll get quite natural, nice shots that look above all realistic.

46
00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:55.180
This is this year's trend, and we like it, because "painting over with color" may be attractive at first glance, but isn't quite normal.

47
00:04:55.180 --> 00:05:13.540
The A56 is somewhere in the middle, so it will give well-balanced and sharp photos. And most importantly, it will be so every time, in any situation. You don't have to worry about whether there's enough light, whether objects are moving: just point the device and shoot — and in 99% of cases you'll get nice shots.

48
00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.000
I'll especially note the very sharp and attractive indoor photos in low light,

49
00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:26.360
which greatly increases functionality in some ordinary life situations, a significant part of which happen precisely indoors.

50
00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:31.760
When shooting video I recommend turning on Super Steady mode to stabilize the video.

51
00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:38.580
Shooting up to 4K at 30 frames per second is supported with very good quality in all situations too.

52
00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:46.440
As for macro photography, the A56 is one of the most impressive inexpensive phones, provided you position the subject well.

53
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:53.900
The app offers professional modes for both photo and video, with some advanced option like Hyperlapse or Slow-Mo.

54
00:05:54.380 --> 00:06:00.660
In detail and sharpness the camera isn't at the S-series level, and it also has no telephoto lens, which is the main complaint,

55
00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.760
but it will give more than good enough photos for the vast majority of users.

56
00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:16.120
As for photo processing, here it's the standard Samsung set, plus erase and edit functions, and all this works pretty well and lets you create interesting content, above all for social media.

57
00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:25.460
Everything is driven by the Exynos 1580 chipset. It's built on a 4-nanometer process, with an operating clock speed of up to 2.9 GHz.

58
00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.180
The chipset has 8 cores, and in the AnTuTu test it scores more than 900 thousand, which is impressive for this class of devices.

59
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:37.200
Nevertheless it's not a gaming phone, so don't expect maximum settings in the most demanding games.

60
00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:43.840
For ordinary users everything else will run fast and stably, with the numerous options offered by Samsung's operating system.

61
00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:50.800
It has One UI 7 and Android 15, with 6 years of software updates guaranteed, and that's more than enough.

62
00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.000
What I didn't like is the phone activation process.

63
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.820
On Samsung it takes longer than necessary in general, but here the phone rebooted twice for some reason,

64
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.800
and then spent almost ten minutes doing something, and only in the end did I manage to register it.

65
00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:09.260
And that's not all: it automatically started downloading 130 GB of updates for various apps.

66
00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.520
So expect that you'll need a few hours from the moment you take it out of the box

67
00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.120
until the phone is ready for use, and that can be annoying.

68
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:22.440
The phone ran fast and stably, and the chipset heats up, but only in more demanding apps.

69
00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:31.160
As for the battery, you can use it very actively all day and you won't drain it, meaning there's almost always a little power left for one more day.

70
00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:36.260
The battery capacity is 5000 mAh, and 45 W charging is supported,

71
00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.900
which means the speed is the same as the S25 Ultra's, and that's great news.

72
00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.360
Samsung finally realized it was time to increase charging speed.

73
00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:50.120
In practice you get 100% charge in about 80 minutes, and about 50% in half an hour.

74
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:58.720
Of course, there are AI features too, though somewhat cut down compared with the S series, but most users hardly use any of it anyway, so there's no need to worry.

75
00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:07.380
Samsung has for years been one of the champions of stability and development of its operating system, so the A56 is also packed with extra features.

76
00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:20.120
For instance, you can use Drag to Share or choose Best Face when shooting portraits, and the home screen has a Now Bar, where you can place important apps or notifications, and we also liked the battery-saving option at night.

77
00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:30.800
There are others too, so you'll have to dig around the settings a bit to unlock everything, because many options aren't that easy to find, and that's one of the problems of advanced and complex operating systems.

78
00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:42.260
Finally, let's not forget that the phone doesn't come with a charger, case or even a screen protector, and our advice is to buy all of that as soon as possible, despite the advanced drop protection the phone provides.

79
00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:52.700
The Samsung Galaxy A56 looks superb, has faster charging and very balanced other specs, a reliable camera and decent speed, and on top of that it's a Samsung.

80
00:08:52.700 --> 00:09:09.280
All this makes a very good offer in the mid-range, at a price of 54,999 dinars for the configuration with 8 GB of RAM and 128 GB of storage and 59,999 dinars for the 256 GB version.